  "notes": {
    "findings": [
      "Partner referrals are 6% of leads but 45% of pipeline (€2.84m) and 18 of 36 won deals, at €242 per SQL.",
      "LinkedIn Ads is the biggest spend (€78k) and the most leads (420), but returns the least pipeline per euro (€7.17) and costs €4,333 per SQL.",
      "LI_AI_Delivery_Q2 spent €41k for 151 leads and 109 MQLs, and produced zero SQLs and zero pipeline.",
      "Case studies are the content that works: 16.0% and 14.3% lead to SQL and 44.9% of all pipeline between them. Both blogs and the AI webinar convert at under 4%.",
      "CTOs and VPs of Engineering convert at about 13%. Developers (2.7%) and marketing managers (0.9%) are 24% of leads and 8% of pipeline."
    ],
    "cleaning": [
      "Removed 12 exact duplicate rows (1,412 to 1,400).",
      "Mapped 18 source spellings to the 6 channels used in the spend file (e.g. 'linkedin', 'LinkedIn' and 'linkedin ads' to LinkedIn Ads; 'SEO' and 'organic' to Organic Search).",
      "Parsed 204 dates in DD/MM/YYYY alongside ISO dates. Day values reach 31 and month values never pass 9, so the format is unambiguous.",
      "Converted 5 deal values stored as text (e.g. '€56,500') to numbers.",
      "Set 58 blank regions to 'Unknown', blank campaigns to '(none)', and fixed job-title casing on 44 raw rows.",
      "Pipeline = deal value on leads that reached Opportunity (open, won or lost). SQL count includes everything at SQL or later."
    ],
    "caveats": [
      "Attribution is single-source first touch. Partner and event leads may have been warmed by paid or content before, and that credit is invisible here.",
      "Won-deal counts outside partners are small (3 to 5 per channel), so revenue by channel is directional.",
      "Leads from August and September haven't had time to progress. September is a partial month (70 leads to 12 Sep).",
      "Spend is a single Jan to Sep total per channel, so there is no monthly cost trend. Organic and outbound spend are as supplied and may not include salaries."
    ],
    "next_steps": [
      "Stop LI_AI_Delivery_Q2 now and move the budget to a partner programme and case-study offers aimed at CTOs and VPs of Engineering.",
      "Make the two case studies the default offer in paid, retargeting and outbound. Retire the blog and webinar as lead magnets for paid.",
      "Report weekly on SQLs, pipeline and pipeline per euro by channel instead of MQLs, which reward LinkedIn volume that never converts."
    ]
  }
}